     "lesson": "THE AGGREGATE IS AN ACCIDENT OF MIX. Whole-job error is only +4.4% uncorrected because large band errors cancel: <1.5m2 is -35.5% (register UNDER-prices small units - actual GBP 697/m2 against a median of GBP 450), 1.5-3m2 is -1.2% (excellent), 3-6m2 is +37.5% and >6m2 is +35.2% (register OVER-prices large units). Per type the spread is -43.6% to +46.9% and only 15 of 31 land within +/-20%. So the register is a good whole-package predictor ONLY where the unit mix is broad, and a poor per-element one outside the 1.5-3m2 band. Both available corrections make this job worse, not better - the raw median was closest. One job is not enough to move a factor built on 273 lines, so nothing in the engine was changed; the band structure, not the supplier factor, is what looks wrong.",
