   "subject": "FILWOOD - Aplus quote in, but BOTH systems now fail the U-value in writing. And the workbook carries another firm's traces. Deadline Thu",
   "body": "Adam,\n Aplus have quoted Filwood too - QT51510 came in this morning. Deadline is Thursday.\n The number looks like good news and is not. But it has settled three arguments, and it has raised one\nthat matters more than the price.\n THE HEADLINE\n Aplus GBP 34,445.91. BSW GBP 46,067.59. That is GBP 11,621.68 apart - and they are not the same scope.\n Aplus say, in three words on page 16: &quot;Panels by others.&quot;\n They have left 46.09 m2 of spandrel, base and ventilation-zone infill out - 37.5% of the elevation.\nIt is visible line by line: every non-glazed aperture is listed as a 32mm opening with no product\nagainst it, and three of ED-06's seven segments have no glass line at all. BSW include all of it, as\n70 flat aluminium panels.\n Break-even is GBP 252.15 per m2 of panel. Below that Aplus is genuinely cheaper, above it BSW is.\n I cannot tell you which. BSW bundle the panels into the element price with no extractable figure,\nAplus exclude them, and our rate register has no panel or spandrel category at all. It needs a price,\nnot an estimate. Please do not let GBP 34,445.91 be read as a saving.\n THE ONE THAT MATTERS MORE\n Page 16, again their words: &quot;Quoted in STII, these will only reach 1.8/1.9 U Value.&quot;\n The drawing schedule asks for 1.0 per element.\n BSW told us the same thing on 24 July in different words - performance met &quot;for glazing only... they are\nnon rebated&quot;. Aplus have now put a number on it. Their standard terms go further still: &quot;Commercial\ndoors and framing will be supplied with a U-Value of up to 3.0&quot;.\n Two independent fabricators, two systems, both saying no. At that point it stops being a supplier\nproblem. A standard commercial shopfront system is not thermally broken to curtain-walling standard and\ndoes not get to 1.0 - which is very probably why the architect specified Aluprof and issued the drawings\nto Aluprof directly in October.\n We have not approached a single Aluprof fabricator. I think the Aluprof specification is not a\nformality to engineer around; it may be the only route to the performance, and if it is, both our\nprices are for the wrong product.\n Aplus also state &quot;STII doors have no formal acoustic test data&quot; - ED-06 needs Rw 32 dB - and &quot;Glass\nquoted has a g value of 0.66&quot; against a required 0.5 to 0.6. That last one is useful: it is the first\nhard number anyone has given us on the g-value, and it confirms neither quote has solar control glass\nin it.\n THREE ARGUMENTS SETTLED\n 1. The sizes. Aplus set out to the trade bill exactly - 4930, 5550, and 6315 x 3105 - and their ED-06\n segments run 300 / 1200 / 700 / 600, which is the dimension string printed on the drawing. So BSW's\n 4850 / 4800 / 6250 are wrong, and our own 3150 for ED-06 is a typo for 3105.\n\n 2. The g-value. 0.66 quoted against 0.5-0.6 required.\n\n 3. Delivery. Aplus: &quot;All orders are priced as Ex-Works&quot;, free only over GBP 5,000 AND within 50 miles of\n Watford. Bristol is about 105 miles. BSW are ex works too and their quote carries no terms page at\n all. Carriage is in neither number.\n\n SOMETHING TO STOP BEFORE THURSDAY\n I ran the job through mary_checks and pointed it at the actual files. The Filwood pricing workbook\ncarries dan.parker@agsurveying.co.uk in its properties, and external links to C:\\Users\\LiamO'Donnell\nand C:\\Users\\Parke through an Outlook cache path.\n That is the same defect that went to Pearce on Georgie's this week. The difference is that Filwood has\nnot gone out yet, so this one we can still catch. Strip it before anything is attached.\n The full run returns 9 failures. Workbook attached - the new &quot;Aplus QT51510&quot; sheet has the line-by-line\ncomparison and every one of Aplus's own qualifications quoted verbatim.\n WHAT I HAVE NOT DONE\n I have not raised a new request. There are 24 open already and you cannot clear those in a day. I have\nadded this to REQ-10, which was already the Filwood decision.\n Nothing has gone to Stepnell.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
