   "body": "Mary - three questions about Barnfield Construction, and they all reduce to \"did it leave\nestimating@\". Nothing here needs a price from you, only a send date.\n\nBarnfield are the largest single-client exposure on my board - GBP 568,576 ex VAT across five\nlive-quoted AdminBase leads - and Fenster has won nothing from them in six enquiries. Their\nestimator Ian Brown keeps asking us to price, so the access is not the problem.\n\n1. BRADSTONE ROAD, Cheetham Hill, Manchester M8 8WA (Barnfield, AdminBase lead 5625,\n   GBP 218,917.29 ex VAT). Ian Brown told Jayk on 11/03/2025 we were joint-top of five quotes at\n   about GBP 378k, with three cheaper at 275/255/249k, and that he was happy for us to value\n   engineer. Harry Grover circulated a revised quote internally on 27/03/2025 - \"Hi both\", to Jayk\n   and Adam, BSW buy at GBP 147,294.62+VAT. The figure now on the CRM row is GBP 218,917, which is\n   about GBP 30k BELOW the cheapest quote we knew about. Then on 01/05/2025 Jayk told BSW\n   \"Bradstone Road: lost on price, you can close this enquiry.\"\n\n   A revision that undercut the field by GBP 30k, and then lost on price, does not add up. There is\n   no send of it to Ian Brown anywhere in commercial@, info@ or jacob@, and jayk@ is a hard 404.\n   DID THAT REVISED QUOTE GO OUT FROM estimating@, and on what date? If it never went, that is the\n   third job this month where our own price stopped inside the building - Chiel and Alkerden being\n   the other two - and it is worth all three being one problem rather than three coincidences.\n\n2. SAME SITE, ELEVEN MONTHS LATER. Vetroseal sent us quote 060676 \"BRADSTONE RD CHEETHAM\" on\n   29/01/2026 and again on 02/02/2026, to info@, estimating@ and commercial@. It is not an old\n   quote re-sent - Vetroseal number sequentially at roughly 27 a day (064635 on 07/07/2026, 065095\n   on 24/07/2026), so 060676 belongs to early 2026; a re-send of a March 2025 quote would be\n   numbered around 052000. So somebody was buying glass for Bradstone Road in late January 2026,\n   and there is no Barnfield correspondence at all in my four mailboxes in 2026.\n\n   WAS BRADSTONE ROAD BEING PRICED AGAIN IN JANUARY 2026, and for whom? The site is certainly live:\n   Manchester permitted a further application on the land on 10/10/2025. If the job came back to us\n   after we lost it, my board is wrong to have it down as dead and Adam should hear that today.\n\n3. THE GRANGE APARTMENTS (Barnfield, lead 7665, GBP 155,388.14 ex VAT, Wirral CH48 4EE). AdminBase\n   has this \"Live - Quoted\" with a value against Ian Brown's deadline of 26/02/2026. The Opportunity\n   Log has the same job with Quote Returned EMPTY and never chased. Adam's rule on hub-77 is that\n   priced-but-never-issued is yours, not a chase - so before anyone rings Ian about it, DID THAT\n   QUOTE GO OUT? I have put the row on Today saying exactly that rather than guessing either way.\n\nTwo things from my side you may want regardless of the above. Barnfield's subcontract terms are\ntighter than most: 2.5% main contractor's discount to be built into the figures, 5% retention,\npayment 45 days from month end, and payment applications by POST only - they state they will not\naccept emailed copies. And Jayk's repricing log mixes VAT bases on the same page: Moston Cash &\nCarry is logged at the inclusive figure, MSM Aerospace at the exclusive one, both penny-exact to\nAdminBase. Anything reconciled against that log needs checking a row at a time.\n\nTheir St Johns Refurbishment in Blackburn is the odd one out - your log figure GBP 58,343.68\nagainst AdminBase GBP 89,968.83 ex VAT on the same enquiry date of 19/06/2025. One is a revision of\nthe other and I cannot tell which is current, so I have told nobody to quote either number.\n\nFull write-up in data/companies/barnfield-construction.md."
